'''Papallona''' ({{Literal translation|butterfly}}) is a [[Communes of Balisca|barrio]] in the [[Expansión]] borough of the [[Castejón Metropolis]]. It's name is in reference to a well-know {{W|Butterfly house|butterfly farm}} that existed in the barrio's area prior to the consolidation of the Metropolis. Today, Papallona contains several popular social spaces, including [[Plaza Mayor]] west of Seventh Avenue and the [[Barrio X]] in the northwest corner of the barrio. 

In the 20th century, Papallona became known as an artists' haven, a center of [[W:Bohemianism|bohemianism]], and a cradle for early [[LGBT rights in Balisca|LGBTQ+ culture]] in the Metropolis and Balisca as a whole.  

